    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment feature for the Spring Boot PetClinic app. When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, they're now assigned a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `SMI-0007`), where `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and `NNNN` is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper that computes `LAST3` (`substring(0,3).toUpperCase()`, guarded for short names) and the sequence as `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, formatted with `%s-%04d`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name (kept out of `OwnerFields`, so it can't be set on input).\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` acceptance test \u2014 verifying `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two sequential owners' numbers differ by exactly 1 \u2014 passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green.",
